+   "files":["src/Uinsure.Policies.Api/Contracts/SellPolicyRequest.cs"],
+   "root_cause":"Same cause as I1. The scale check at SellPolicyRequest.cs:62 overflows for very large negative amounts, so Validate throws before the domain's SELL-7 check at src/Uinsure.Policies.Domain/Policies/Policy.cs:110-113 (`amount <= 0` gives 422) can run. The agreed rules give a different answer. docs/requirements.md:63 says SELL-7: 'The policy amount must be greater than 0, else 422'. The H6 ruling (docs/plans/active/build.dag.yaml:168) makes only 'more than 2 decimal places, or above 1,000,000.00' a 400. A very large negative with at most 2 decimal places is neither, so by the agreed interpretation it should still be the 422 SELL-7 it was in F1. F1b's own acceptance asks for 'No behaviour change' (build.dag.yaml:164). Fix direction: make the shape check safe for every decimal value a request can bind, so it can never throw. Amounts within 2 decimal places, however negative, should then go on to the domain and get the SELL-7 422. Keep the existing 400s for more than 2 decimal places and for amounts above 1,000,000.00. If David would rather treat a very large negative as a 400 shape error, that changes the H6 ruling and needs his decision, not a builder's.",
